body:
@artaommahe, I just checked the `jest API` again, and the current `tick()` behavior is not a bug. It is the same with `jest.advanceTimersByTime`.
```
jest.useFakeTimers();
const callback = jest.fn();
waitTwice(callback);

jest.advanceTimersByTime();

expect(callback).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
`
jest.advanceTimersByTime();

expect(callback).toHaveBeenCalled();
```

will be the same behavior with `tick`.

So what you want is a `fakeAsync version` of `runOnlyPendingTimers` which will not invoke `nested setTimeout`?
